# Claims in someone else's kit (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "Claims in someone else's kit"): you're claiming
# only when you pick the claim. The look decides it (its score is shown before you pick); a passed
# look waves you through this post, and buys nothing else. The true answer costs nothing.

conv post.bastion.claim
for post:bastion
when kit:in_kit & !caught
topic "Don't you know me?"
prio quest
voice bastion

node start
  say No, and I know every face on this post's board. You're in our kit, so tell me: which unit, which section, and who signs for your rations? Take your time. I've got all day and a rifle.
  > @claim One of yours. Let me through. -> passed | caught   check look bastion 2
  > @truth Took it off a dead man. I'm not yours. -> honest
  > @leave Forget it. I'll go back the way I came. -> hub

node passed
  say Fine. Must be the new draft down from the hills. Go on, and keep your head down past the sandbags. We're short of heads as it is.
  do call:post_wave
  > @back1 Thanks. One more thing. -> hub

node caught
  say Hands on the barrier. Nobody in Bastion forgets their own section. That kit goes back to the stores it came from, and you get a page in the log.
  > @back2 Understood. Hands on the barrier. -> hub

node honest
  say At least you said so. That's more than most do. Take it off before somebody less patient asks you the same question with the safety off.
  > @back3 I will. Can I ask you something else? -> hub

# Bastion's word at the wire: three words, one of them today's (changed at the 05:30 shift and read
# on Bastion's secure net). The right one counts at the next look; a wrong one is caught at once.
# Not knowing it is no crime: the look runs without it.
conv post.bastion.word
for post:bastion
when kit:in_kit & !caught
topic "I've got the word."
prio quest
voice bastion

node start
  say Then say it. It changed at half five this morning, same as every morning, and every post had it read out on the net. One word, and say it quietly.
  > @w1 {wire:1}. -> said   do wire:1
  > @w2 {wire:2}. -> said   do wire:2
  > @w3 {wire:3}. -> said   do wire:3
  > @none I haven't had today's word. -> without

node said
  jump caught -> wrong
  say That'll do for the wire. Now your unit, your section, and who signs for your rations.
  > @claim One of yours. Let me through. -> passed | refused   check look bastion 2
  > @leave I'll wait here. -> hub

node without
  say Then you'd better have a face I know, because the word is how we tell our own from people wearing our jackets. Unit?
  > @claim2 One of yours. Let me through. -> passed | refused   check look bastion 2
  > @leave2 I'll wait here, then. -> hub

node passed
  say Go on. Keep the word to yourself and don't say it anywhere near the toll lorries: they listen to our net. It changes again at half five.
  do call:post_wave
  > @back1 Thanks. One more thing. -> hub

node refused
  say No. Word or no word, you don't know your own section and I don't know your face. Hands on the barrier. That kit goes back where it came from.
  > @back2 Understood. -> hub

node wrong
  say Wrong word. That's yesterday's, or the Red Hand's guess at it. Wrong word, wrong kit, and your hands on the barrier, now.
  > @back3 All right. Hands on the barrier. -> hub

conv post.redhand.claim
for post:redhand
when kit:in_kit & !caught
topic "Come on, you know me."
prio quest
voice redhand

node start
  say Do I? I know every face on this road, and every name the crews have handed out since the lorry first went across it. Yours isn't one of them. Whose crew, and what do they call you?
  > @claim I'm with a crew up north. Wave me on. -> passed | caught   check look redhand 2
  > @truth Found the armband. Thought it'd help. -> honest
  > @leave Forget I asked. -> hub

node passed
  say Huh. Must be one of the new lot off the hill road. Go on, then. Next time you pay like everyone, armband or no armband.
  do call:post_wave
  > @back1 Cheers. One more thing. -> hub

node caught
  say Lads! Dress-up day. This one's wearing our colours and doesn't know whose. Armband off, if you please, and turn your pockets out while you're at it.
  > @back2 Fair enough. It's coming off. -> hub

node honest
  say It might, too. Not here. Here we count the armbands, and every one of them has a name in the book. Take it off before somebody else counts it.
  > @back3 Fair. Can I ask you something else? -> hub
